#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
V4-A3.15
Directional Source-versus-Transit Attribution

This stage analyzes the frozen A3 input features and the frozen A3.13 branch
scores without training or changing model weights.

Validation is the only split used to rank directional/source-transit proxy
metrics. The development-comparison test split is used only to describe the
already identified hard-normal cases.

Validation router roles:
  benign_active_source
  benign_inactive_router
  true_attacker
  attack_legitimate_active
  attack_other_router

Saved feature semantics:
  0  ifd_in_norm
  1  ifd_out_norm
  2  input_flit_count_norm
  3  output_flit_count_norm
  4:9   in_count_norm_[local,north,east,south,west]
  9:14  out_count_norm_[local,north,east,south,west]
  14:19 ifd_in_norm_[local,north,east,south,west]
  19:24 ifd_out_norm_[local,north,east,south,west]

Derived quantities are explicitly labeled as proxies. They do not replace
missing dataset semantics such as a direct source/transit/valid-port label.

No threshold search, no classifier fitting, no test selection, and no training
occur.
"""

